      <span class="eyebrow">About Amla Powder</span>
      <h2 class="h-sec">What is Amla <span class="it" style="color:var(--c)">powder?</span></h2>
      <p>Amla (<i>Phyllanthus emblica</i>), also called Indian gooseberry or Amalaki, is a round, pale-green fruit with a bright, sour taste. It has been eaten fresh, pickled, dried and powdered across India for generations and holds a central place in Ayurveda.</p><p>Veda Apothecary Amla Powder contains one ingredient — Amla fruit — with no additives, fillers or preservatives. It is a natural source of Vitamin C: a 5 g serving lists 25 mg, which is 28% of the Daily Value, on the Supplement Facts panel. Because Amla is so sour, most people mix it into juice, sparkling water or smoothies rather than plain water.</p>
      <table class="facts"><caption class="sr-only">Amla Powder key facts</caption><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Botanical name</th><td><i>Phyllanthus emblica</i></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Plant part</th><td>Fruit</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Net weight</th><td>8 oz (227 g)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Servings per container</th><td>about 45</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ingredients</th><td>One — fruit powder only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Origin</th><td>Product of India</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Distributed by</th><td>Old Soul Goods Inc.</td></tr></tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

